{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-105752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=2,$ and ${x}_{4}=-1$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-105752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=2,$ and ${x}_{4}=-1,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x-(-1)) \\\\  & =1(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x+1) & =1({x}^{2}-4x+4)({x}^{2}-x-2) \\\\  & =1({x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+8x+4{x}^{2}-4x-8) \\\\  & =1({x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-105752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f4ac7e10ccd67cb06df9ae17ba4a61cc2e6cdb5724d7425e52d7d7b3165cb14"} {"question" "q-105752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-105752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+12x-8"] ["math" "{x}^{4}+5{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+12x-8"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-12x-8"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+4x-8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-105752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+4x-8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-319855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=3,$ and ${x}_{4}=-4$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,108$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-319855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=3,$ and ${x}_{4}=-4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-3)(x-3)(x-3)(x-(-4)) \\\\  & =(x-3)(x-3)(x-3)(x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)(x-3)(x-3)(x+4) & =({x}^{2}-6x+9)({x}^{2}+x-12) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+72x+9{x}^{2}+9x-108 \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+81x-108.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+81x-108.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-319855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f4ac7e10ccd67cb06df9ae17ba4a61cc2e6cdb5724d7425e52d7d7b3165cb14"} {"question" "q-319855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-319855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x^4-5x^3-9x^2+81x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/assets/6a39af16798593716291ab84bfff4460279420f493bd10959782312187f0bf44.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,72$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm \\text{i}$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 6\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-\\text{i}))(x-\\text{i})(x-(-6\\text{i}))(x-6\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2(x+\\text{i})(x-\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i})(x-6\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+\\text{i})(x-\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i})(x-6\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+(\\text{i}-\\text{i})x-{\\text{i}}^{2})({x}^{2}+(6\\text{i}-6\\text{i})x-36{\\text{i}}^{2}) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+1)({x}^{2}+36) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{4}+36{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}+36) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{4}+37{x}^{2}+36) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{4}+74{x}^{2}+72 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{4}+74{x}^{2}+72.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f4ac7e10ccd67cb06df9ae17ba4a61cc2e6cdb5724d7425e52d7d7b3165cb14"} {"question" "q-320185" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320185" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x^4+74x^2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/assets/4f960f00fbcbde79dee3603112ed08e8c34cf87b3ccbe781ee5acbf61a4482fd.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,52$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=-2\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and ${x}_{3,4}=1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-2+3\\text{i}))(x-(-2-3\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-(-2+3\\text{i}))(x-(-2-3\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+4x+4+9)({x}^{2}-2x+1+1) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+4x+13)({x}^{2}-2x+2) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+8x+13{x}^{2}-26x+26) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-18x+26) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}-36x+52 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}-36x+52.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f4ac7e10ccd67cb06df9ae17ba4a61cc2e6cdb5724d7425e52d7d7b3165cb14"} {"question" "q-320235" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320235" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x^4+4x^3+14x^2-36x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/assets/58136b4140d772431a823b66b03ebfa95bd51816e4df9be7f2401c29c97a5495.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,36$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=2,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=-1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-3))(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+3)(x-2)(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}-2x+3x-6)({x}^{2}-x(-1-\\text{i})-x(-1+\\text{i})+(-1+\\text{i})(-1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+x-6)\\,({x}^{2}+2x+2) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+2x-6{x}^{2}-12x-12) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-30x-36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-30x-36.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f4ac7e10ccd67cb06df9ae17ba4a61cc2e6cdb5724d7425e52d7d7b3165cb14"} {"question" "q-320276" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"} {"question" "q-320276" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x^4+9x^3-6x^2-30x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070073/state.json" "file_sha256" "58645ea22d37377f088e57032d8da941471785249491338e9ec9cfa946330863"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2437 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
